        "text": "ABOUT THE MAJOR\nThe English major is ideal for students who love literature, language, and creative writing. Completing this major will prepare students to enter a single subject credential program to become a high school English teacher, and it will also prepare students for a range of other careers in editing, journalism, law, library science, publishing, and many other fields.\n\nMAJOR ELECTIVE REQUIREMENT\nStudents will select at least 12 additional units courses from the list of approved courses in the Catalog.\n\n﻿**Agreement does not include all required courses for the major at FPU**\nThis agreement lists courses that are prerequisites or may be completed prior to transfer to satisfy major requirements. All transfer courses must be completed with a grade of C- or better, and students must complete a minimum of 18 units in the major at FPU. Please contact an academic advisor to discuss the recommended sequence of courses, including courses that may count for both GE and major requirements. To view the full degree requirements, please refer to the Undergraduate Catalog: https://catalog.fresno.edu/index.php.",
